{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975893-brainstorming-for-an-angelic-pantheon","id":975893,"title":"Brainstorming for an Angelic Pantheon","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-25T02:52:53-07:00","id":975893,"title":"Brainstorming for an Angelic Pantheon","content":"Thinking about how to make an Abrahamic Pantheon work elsewhere led me to settle on the idea that the best approach would be the Angels as the 'Gods,' rather than the monotheistic creator Himself; it offers more options for character creation, neatly dodges the possible offense of &quot;my player character is the Other Messiah,&quot; and still allows a group to approach Abrahamic myth in an interesting way that hits all three major faiths within it. <br /> <br /> My preliminary thoughts are that the Pantheon and their Scions (who are always Chosen or Created, never Born) work to uphold YHVH's will, but have little or no contact with Him and are left largely to fend for themselves. The Virtue pair should have something to do with service and individualism (so that our buddy Lucifer can be seen as a rogue extreme operating at the unbalanced end of the spectrum), while I'm struggling with a distinct PSP because we lack any examples right now. There might be room to do a divide of some sort to reflect the original religious texts in comparison to the occultism we see with John Dee and later figures, but that might be over-seasoning the pot. Probably stick to the major Archangels, at least to start.<br /> <br /> Any thoughts? Do you think this idea is worth pursuing once we see more of the rules?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T04:10:49-07:00","id":975905,"title":"","content":"There is already a thread which created the pantheon members and had the beginnings of a PSP for 1E on this board.<br /> <br /> Most people agree that it is... generally a bad idea, to have an Abrahamic pantheon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","name":"Crying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12300_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T10:28:13-07:00","id":976002,"title":"","content":"Well, an Angelic Pantheon would have to make some compromises- first and foremost, recognizing that other gods do exist. I don't think that it can't be done or that it is a bad idea by its very basis, but it requires some work to fit to the setting. I imagine it would be a mysterious and isolated Pantheon, in which the angels and scions themselves don't really know where God is- there is this hierarchy of angels, and each rank leads to another, and another and another- up to Michael, and he doesn't tell anything. Making God hidden behind layers of hierarchy and bureaucracy could be, I think, interesting path instead of the regular &quot;God is gone and nobody knows where&quot;. Also, it should be able for Scions to be Born of angels- it is just a taboo in the Pantheon, which generally ends with punishment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T10:36:29-07:00","id":976007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975893-brainstorming-for-an-angelic-pantheon?p=976002#post976002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, it should be able for Scions to be Born of angels- it is just a taboo in the Pantheon, which generally ends with punishment.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bad memories of the Nephilim.<br /> <br /> Hm. It could be that for whatever reason angelic-born Scions often end up with supernatural markings, much like Titan Scions. Most common would be gigantism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T10:38:24-07:00","id":976009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975893-brainstorming-for-an-angelic-pantheon?p=976007#post976007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Bad memories of the Nephilim.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> whom? was it some kind of fan project or something?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T10:53:06-07:00","id":976014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975893-brainstorming-for-an-angelic-pantheon?p=976009#post976009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">whom? was it some kind of fan project or something?</div> </div> </div> </div>In Biblical apocrypha, the Nephilim were the children of angels and humanity, described as giants, who were wiped out by the Flood. When you mentioned birthing Scions was a taboo for angels, my mind jumped to the Nephilim as the explanation why.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T11:05:38-07:00","id":976019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975893-brainstorming-for-an-angelic-pantheon?p=976014#post976014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In Biblical apocrypha, the Nephilim were the children of angels and humanity, described as giants, who were wiped out by the Flood. When you mentioned birthing Scions was a taboo for angels, my mind jumped to the Nephilim as the explanation why.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I know about the biblical Nephilim- it's just that when you said &quot;bad memories&quot; I've thought that there was some sort of fan project who didn't went out well. What gave you bad memories from them? (or that I have totally misinterpreted what you've said and you meant that the angels have bad memories, which totally makes sense when I think about that..)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T11:07:19-07:00","id":976020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975893-brainstorming-for-an-angelic-pantheon?p=976019#post976019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, I know about the biblical Nephilim- it's just that when you said &quot;bad memories&quot; I've thought that there was some sort of fan project who didn't went out well. What gave you bad memories from them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I didn't mean bad memories for me, I meant for the angels.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T12:21:24-07:00","id":976045,"title":"","content":"I think you are taking this in a good direction (angels only, no direct children). I would lean heavily on a take of &quot;...no other gods before Me&quot; that allows for the existence of other gods without a need to destroy them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1011-phgraves","name":"PHGraves","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1011_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T12:50:40-07:00","id":976057,"title":"","content":"As an idea, perhaps this could focus more on the plurality of the Elohim rather than a singular creator-God and His angelic servants? <br /> <br /> For the PSP, would there be room in there for a pillar-of-salt type thing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T12:04:42-07:00","id":977877,"title":"","content":"You might find some useful inspiration in the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/In_Nomine_(role-playing_game)\" target=\"_blank\">In Nomine rpg</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1885-crackedman","name":"CrackedMan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1885_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T08:20:38-07:00","id":978421,"title":"","content":"I posted this on the kickstarter page so I figured id copy it over here as well. People seem to like it so far.<br /> <br /> &quot;Probably late to the party but I wanted to chime in on the Abrahamic faith.<br /> As a Christian I honestly feel the best way to represent God would but using EI from the Canaanite Pantheon. Some christian fans simply want to be represented while others have said they try to correlate God to fate. I think if we are to be represented fairly then we need him to be equal to other gods in other pantheons rather than making him a unknown power that supremely rules over all. As seemingly insulting as it would be to say the &quot;there is only one true god&quot; statement is false it would be equally insulting to say that in a world where all myths and faiths are true that for some reason the most modernly accepted one is more powerful than all the rest.<br /> <br /> Others have mentioned that they could portray EI as getting too big for his britches and stating to his followers that he is the only true god but ultimately that doesn't even need to be the case. What would paint &quot;God&quot; in a more negative light? Saying that he is a megalomaniac who believes he is the true and only god or saying that he is a god who rarely speaks and has zealot followers who take his rarely spoken words farther than he intended. I'd prefer the 2nd one because it ultimately paints mortals as flawed rather than God and fits the theme.<br /> <br /> All I can ask is pleeease do not make a Angelic Pantheon canon. I see Scion as a far more sophisticated beast than that. Angels in a pantheon just really doesnt make much sense and it seems really forced rather than graceful. On top of forcing them into only having chosen scions or being destroyed by the mega God above them (who disapproves of nephalem) it just seems like it messes with the formula of scion way too much. Trust me, I'm a huge fan of Wic-Div and the Lucifer character is one of my favorites but I really don't want to see Christianity portrayed in a way where our angels are as powerful as everyone elses gods. That just feels wrong in a system like Scion that tries to equally rep every culture and faith.<br /> <br /> And finally, I just trust Neall to do a good of the Canaanite Pantheon as well as Scion as a whole. As someone who followed Scion the whole time Neall has been given authority over it I trust that he cares enough about the game and it's world to represent it properly. I know there are some people who still want the Angelic Pantheon and I'm sure people will make one asap when the game comes out but I reaaaalllly don't want to have that be the canon place of Christianity in &quot;The World&quot;. Neall has mentioned how badly he wants to do the Canaanite Pantheon and ultimately I think it would be pretty dang hard to do that properly without atleast nodding towards &quot;God&quot; when it comes to EI... you know, the most high, and the king of the pantheon.<br /> <br /> Hopefully that doesn't come off as harsh to anyone out there and hopefully others agree.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T08:33:06-07:00","id":978427,"title":"","content":"I had no familiarity with the Canaanite pantheon, so I had to look it up, but wow that seems perfect. I definitely think this is the best way to go and to have the Judeo-Christian &quot;God&quot; be a mortal spin-off faction that took El and went and made him a solo act.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1885-crackedman","name":"CrackedMan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1885_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T13:46:07-07:00","id":978595,"title":"","content":"While I would love to get a Canaanite Pantheon, the last thing I want to see is &quot;El as the Judeo-Christian God&quot;. There must be a better way to deal with the &quot;monotheistic paradox&quot; of All Myths are True other than that, especially it doesn't really solve the paradox. I think that I would like to see how the Loa are presented in the new edition before making any advances about any &quot;Abrahamic Pantheon&quot;, but I don't think that having an angelic pantheon is a problem by its core, although I don't believe it would be canon. I understand the problems people may have about that, and I respect their opinions, so I'm not going to make a big post or something like that.<br /> <br /> But please- no &quot;El is the Abrahamic God&quot;. It would make cringe so hard I'll crack my teeth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T14:06:38-07:00","id":978609,"title":"","content":"I would also suggest making their Virtues at least partially combat related. Angels weren't friendly creatures, they were warriors who got sent out when God wanted to drop the hammer on somebody. If an Arch Angel showed up, it was the Biblical equivalent to God launching a nuke.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Personally</i> I think Akhetatten already satisfies this pantheon just fine, as there appears to be a great deal of correlation between the Titan of Light, it's avatar (Aten), it's servants (who actually include angels), and the Abrahamic faiths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-29-2016, 05:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T20:18:01-07:00","id":978815,"title":"","content":"I was thinking the Virtues could be Piety (which is really more humility and compassion combined with the ability to interpret God's will) and Judgement (the ability to judge others and oneself by a clear moral standard, and not succumb to bias when carrying out boons or banes). They conflict when Piety would obstruct the process of Judgement (the story of Job comes to mind, as Isaac was completely innocent and by the call of Judgement, should be rewarded) or where Judgement would make the insights of Piety difficult to stomach (Jonah had a very good reason to hate Nineveh, so it's not a surprise he wasn't happy about warning it of calamity and letting it avoid destruction).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 09-29-2016, 11:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T12:36:21-07:00","id":979202,"title":"","content":"I think you're onto something there, Leliel. <br /> <br /> To migrate the info I posted in the Monotheism thread to a more appropriate environment...<br /> <br /> Regarding the original topic, the roster sounds like...<br /> Michael<br /> Gabriel<br /> Lucifer<br /> Raphael<br /> Uriel<br /> Ramiel<br /> Raguel<br /> Sariel<br /> Metatron<br /> <br /> That's 9. The first three are mentioned in the Bible proper, while the next five are listed in the Book of Enoch. Metatron is more of a mystery and seems more tied to the Talmud. Reviewing the original Scion game, the pantheons ranged from 12 at the most to as little as 7. So, technically, you have a full roster right there. There is another list that has Jophiel, Zadkiel, and Camael for other additions or alternate names for the first nine. And, of course, more could be added, either from In Nominee or just coming up with more on your own. <br /> <br /> Now, there was a three faction idea that was forming between the different angels. One idea was to have a divide between the more canon angels and the more angels of the latter occultic traditions. Meanwhile, the third faction could be composed of 'newer' angels, scions that have reached 'godhood' or perhaps be composed of the Nephilim briefly mentioned in Genesis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6942-simison","name":"simison","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6942_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T13:57:33-07:00","id":979251,"title":"","content":"Metatron should be a Scion who rose to &quot;godhood&quot;, considering his possible origin as Enoch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T16:43:25-07:00","id":979325,"title":"","content":"And the other five that are referenced in Enoch?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6942-simison","name":"simison","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6942_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T16:59:53-07:00","id":979938,"title":"","content":"This may not be a popular idea, but I don't think it is possible to make a Monotheistic religion into a more traditional pantheon. Not saying monotheism can't be a force in the world, but is not a direct pantheon, in general monotheistic religions just don't follow the formula set here as a general guide. Almost all the myths seem to revolve around God's followers rather than God, and whether Jesus was a Holy figure/a Messiah/ or a Prophet matters very much on the belief never mind particular sects among those religions. <br /> <br /> The truth is God's mantle is at least said to be Omnipotent and putting that to numbers here doesn't capture His myth. I would say God works with &quot;Sorcerers&quot; or humans who through faith can use the PSP however Origins makes it work. They are powerful, but God does prefer to use subtlety mostly when communicating with His followers and even when blatant often sends a messenger, His burning bush days are over.<br /> <br /> That said I still feel His most faithful are still a force to be reckoned with and are varied. There is evidence He is connected to Canaan and Amun but not overwhelmingly so. (Up to interpretation of ST basically) His people are varied and some live peacefully among those who worship other Gods and some make War. Some Gods acknowledge Him others do not. Perhaps He is stretched to wide, or He really is an omnipotent God whose motivations are unclear even when written down, to the point Wars are fought between His followers over minutiae. <br /> <br /> Basically give his followers a powerful PSP, And perhaps the virtue of Obedience but it wars with itself because each faction, each individual has various ideas about what His will is, and He rarely gets involved directly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11938-3comrades","name":"3Comrades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T09:11:47-07:00","id":982160,"title":"","content":"If I were trying to design an angelic pantheon, I'd go more Solomonic/Goetic/Enochian. Rather than have individual deities, make them more a list of categories of type of angel, and then give a primary example of each. That way, you're less tied to any other pantheon and can include huge variety. The angels wouldn't be servants of any particular deity - though they may venerate some supreme supernal sovereign in the abstract - but rather a host of lesser gods and aspects.<br /> <br /> And hey, angels also announce divine births all the time. Samson, for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T16:58:32-07:00","id":983601,"title":"","content":"i'm not trying to knock anyone that gives an angelic pantheon a try, but i'd leave angels as legendary creatures and let scion focus on the story of actual organized pantheons from places that aren't israel, because biblical-focused fiction is really starting to annoy me. most &quot;christian&quot; films are particularly guilty of this, as they don't even give other &quot;myths&quot; room to actually move beyond being strawman religious idols.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/885-bwgustaf","name":"bwgustaf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T18:03:36-07:00","id":983651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bwgustaf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975893-brainstorming-for-an-angelic-pantheon?p=983601#post983601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i'm not trying to knock anyone that gives an angelic pantheon a try, but i'd leave angels as legendary creatures and let scion focus on the story of actual organized pantheons from places that aren't israel, because biblical-focused fiction is really starting to annoy me. most &amp;quot;christian&amp;quot; films are particularly guilty of this, as they don't even give other &amp;quot;myths&amp;quot; room to actually move beyond being strawman religious idols.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd love to see where you're finding good urban fantasy with Abrahamic trappings, because outside of two niche roleplaying games from the 90s I've got nothing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T18:04:56-07:00","id":983652,"title":"","content":"The only urban fantasy I recall reading that had any angelic stuff was The Dresden Files.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T19:19:47-07:00","id":983683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975893-brainstorming-for-an-angelic-pantheon?p=983651#post983651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd love to see where you're finding good urban fantasy with Abrahamic trappings, because outside of two niche roleplaying games from the 90s I've got nothing.</div> </div> </div> </div> Trappings aren't the problem. The problem is people pushing the concept that angels have to be more powerful then everything else. you could just as easily create an angelic path that does exactly what angels are expected to do as making angelic gods, but instead people keep pushing the narrative that if your name isn't Apollyon or Michael you really aren't doing the material justice. it's the fact that christian fiction won't settle for just being good fiction but that it automatically has to be on top of everything else the mythological world has to offer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/885-bwgustaf","name":"bwgustaf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T19:31:05-07:00","id":983688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bwgustaf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975893-brainstorming-for-an-angelic-pantheon?p=983683#post983683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Trappings aren't the problem. The problem is people pushing the concept that angels have to be more powerful then everything else. you could just as easily create an angelic path that does exactly what angels are expected to do as making angelic gods, but instead people keep pushing the narrative that if your name isn't Apollyon or Michael you really aren't doing the material justice. it's the fact that christian fiction won't settle for just being good fiction but that it automatically has to be on top of everything else the mythological world has to offer.</div> </div> </div> </div>And... where, exactly, has a single person in this thread said these angels would be better than everyone else in The World?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T20:03:06-07:00","id":983708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>3Comrades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975893-brainstorming-for-an-angelic-pantheon?p=979938#post979938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This may not be a popular idea, but I don't think it is possible to make a Monotheistic religion into a more traditional pantheon. Not saying monotheism can't be a force in the world, but is not a direct pantheon, in general monotheistic religions just don't follow the formula set here as a general guide. Almost all the myths seem to revolve around God's followers rather than God, and whether Jesus was a Holy figure/a Messiah/ or a Prophet matters very much on the belief never mind particular sects among those religions.<br /> <br /> The truth is God's mantle is at least said to be Omnipotent and putting that to numbers here doesn't capture His myth. I would say God works with &quot;Sorcerers&quot; or humans who through faith can use the PSP however Origins makes it work. They are powerful, but God does prefer to use subtlety mostly when communicating with His followers and even when blatant often sends a messenger, His burning bush days are over.<br /> <br /> That said I still feel His most faithful are still a force to be reckoned with and are varied. There is evidence He is connected to Canaan and Amun but not overwhelmingly so. (Up to interpretation of ST basically) His people are varied and some live peacefully among those who worship other Gods and some make War. Some Gods acknowledge Him others do not. Perhaps He is stretched to wide, or He really is an omnipotent God whose motivations are unclear even when written down, to the point Wars are fought between His followers over minutiae.<br /> <br /> Basically give his followers a powerful PSP, And perhaps the virtue of Obedience but it wars with itself because each faction, each individual has various ideas about what His will is, and He rarely gets involved directly.</div> </div> </div> </div>This post, right here. It assumes that god's mantle should Omnipotent which isn't even part of actual angelic lore. it's an idea proposed by thomas aquinas to &quot;prove&quot; that the gods of other nations are inferior to the lord, which not all christians believe prefering instead to focus on his knowledge and benelovence instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/885-bwgustaf","name":"bwgustaf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T23:01:47-07:00","id":983773,"title":"","content":"My big issue with an angel pantheon is that mythology already has the children of angels, and the Nephilim seem more like their own race than they do actual scions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T23:40:11-07:00","id":983787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975893-brainstorming-for-an-angelic-pantheon?p=983652#post983652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only urban fantasy I recall reading that had any angelic stuff was The Dresden Files.</div> </div> </div> </div>Neil Gaiman's Neverwhere too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T08:10:37-07:00","id":984884,"title":"","content":"Me and a friend of mine both started doing something similar to this when <i>Scion</i> seemed close to silent on monotheistic religions...<br /> <br /> The pantheon might not just include angels and archangels and the like, but also such figures as the Grim Reaper and the saints. Folklore combined angels and saints alongside the old gods much more than most people realize--St. Patrick banished Crom Cruach, Ankou was blinded by St. Peter, there's even a Russian folktale where the Devil and the god Perun share a hut with an old peasant. <br /> <br /> Then you have Djinns, dragons, giants, the sea monster Leviathan (slain by the Archangel Raphael) and Ziz and Behemoth, not to mention the mountain of relics to find--you'd have a lot to work with.<br /> <br /> Of course, I'd suggest holding off on developing this further until the first book (maybe even the second) comes out, if only to make sure to fit it into the game line better (and make sure the writers for <i>Scion</i> 2e don't cover something similar).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1868-hellovg","name":"hellovg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"165"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T01:28:23-07:00","id":985316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975893-brainstorming-for-an-angelic-pantheon?p=983773#post983773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My big issue with an angel pantheon is that mythology already has the children of angels, and the Nephilim seem more like their own race than they do actual scions.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Genesis 6:4 &quot;The Nephilim<span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> were in the earth in those days, and also after that, when the sons of God came in unto the daughters of men, and they bore children to them; the same were the mighty men that were of old, the men of renown.&quot;<br /> <br /> Sounds like Scions to me.</span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T01:32:31-07:00","id":985318,"title":"","content":"My biggest question is whether you're using Lucifer, and the apocryphal (or semi-apocryphal depending on how literally you take the Book of Revelation) Christian myth of a fallen rebel angel enemy of God.<br /> <br /> Or if you're using Samael, and favoring the Jewish lore of Satan as a loyal agent of G-d who's job is to test, tempt, and prosecute mankind.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T11:05:17-07:00","id":985518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975893-brainstorming-for-an-angelic-pantheon?p=985316#post985316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Genesis 6:4 &quot;The Nephilim<span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> were in the earth in those days, and also after that, when the sons of God came in unto the daughters of men, and they bore children to them; the same were the mighty men that were of old, the men of renown.&quot;<br /> <br /> Sounds like Scions to me.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In traditional interpretations Nephelim and the children of angels are not normal humans gifted with extraordinary powers, they wear the inhuman countenance of their forebearers openly, and would more closely resemble a human with titanblood. The scion-esque individuals in the bible are not the children of angels, they're descendant of important family lines, basically equivalent to Aragorn being of the line of Numenor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T11:18:16-07:00","id":985533,"title":"","content":"Solana is pretty correct. In Jewish lore, the Nephilim weren't simply superhuman, they were monstrous, possibly even giants, and <i>this was not a good thing.</i><br /> <br /> To lay with the Daughters of Eve (and interfere with human development) was a grave sin that condemned the Watchers, in an eerie echo of the myth of Prometheus, for they brought civilization (and magic) to the human race and were then made anathema for their acts. The Nephilim themselves may well have cannibalized humanity in massive blood orgies and ruled with an iron fist, everything that makes them sound like titanspawn rather than the proper scions.<br /> <br /> The long-dead corpses of the Nephilim are the Rephaim, who are horrifying undead giants, too.<br /> <br /> Now, me, personally, I like the Countercultural interpretation that says that what the Watchers did was fantastic (I'm all for bringing the light of civilization), but that requires you to be okay with going <i>against</i> the will of the Abrahamic god.<br /> <br /> ~<br /> <br /> Really, if you want to include Judaic stuff, you should go back to Canaan, which was the ultimate root of the Abrahamic faith. Look at Asherah and Baal and the other gods that used to be of import in the Kingdom of Israel, you could tell quite a story with that. There's a whole story right there in the bloody, brutal suppression of their temples and faiths in the state of Israel, the direct conflict with the Babylonian pantheon, and more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":5226,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","user":"Jachra","date":". 10-11-2016, 02:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T13:34:06-07:00","id":985635,"title":"","content":"Certainly, there are ancient ties among the Canaanite, Babylonian, and Egyptian Pantheons that are essentially antagonistic to the Israeli God; and a proper treatment of an angelic \u201cPantheon\u201d should acknowledge that. In particular, the relationship between the Hebrew and Canaanite mythologies tends to be somewhat similar to the relationship between the Zoroastrian and Indian mythologies, where each viewed the other's gods as demons.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure it would be a Pantheon, though \u2014 not in the sense of having the Hero-&gt;Demigod-&gt;God thing. Angels as Immortal (mostly Demigod-level, sometimes God-level) servants of a \u201chigher god\u201d who is on par with the \u201chigher gods\u201d who head up numerous Pantheons like the Orisha, Loa, Vedic, etc.? Sure! Mortal priests and prophets empowered by an \u201cAbrahamic faith\u201d PSP? No problem! Even the occasional Chosen \u201cHero\u201d is fine (see Sampson), as long as she never transitions to Demigod status while she's alive: arguably, there's more of a need for Sampson-like judges and angelic hosts in a setting where Heroes and Demigods of the Pantheons are running around. But there should be a sharp divide between the human-dominated Origin/Hero tiers on the one hand and the angel-dominated Demigod/God tiers on the other; and even transitioning from Origin to Hero or from Demigod to God should be rare.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T05:48:17-07:00","id":987211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975893-brainstorming-for-an-angelic-pantheon?p=985318#post985318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My biggest question is whether you're using Lucifer, and the apocryphal (or semi-apocryphal depending on how literally you take the Book of Revelation) Christian myth of a fallen rebel angel enemy of God.<br /> <br /> Or if you're using Samael, and favoring the Jewish lore of Satan as a loyal agent of G-d who's job is to test, tempt, and prosecute mankind.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The two do not have to be exclusive. Remember that this is supposed to be a fictionalized version of these myths. So if Samael is an angel who's purpose is to prosecute (I think the word Satan can litterally be translated as Accuser) humans for their sins, and at the end of The World, God takes the people who have not rejected him to heaven and forgives their sins, what is the natural thing for Samael to do? He is Satan. He is the Accuser of mankind. Odds are that he's not going to sit idly and watch his ability to exercise his purview disappear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1g_IC644YJoiVAm6ngqcBmsQtff2YYtd3pDbZpaOxx4o\" target=\"_blank\">My Exalted Character Creation Tool may be downloaded here.</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1086797-demac-s-exalted-character-creation-tool\" target=\"_blank\">The thread talking about the tool can be found here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1136654-exalted-seats-of-power\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted: Seats of Power is a homebrewed manse creation system.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1oaq3wk7lJKZ022SUA4iPfGzMpmBTNXlM\" target=\"_blank\">I have a rewrite of the craft system which can be downloaded here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1070312-i-got-my-book-it-s-super-fancy-and-i-can-t-read-the-cover/page2\" target=\"_blank\">I like the Mesoamerican look</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2346-demac","name":"Demac","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"385"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T06:20:57-07:00","id":987222,"title":"","content":"Right, but in Judaic Lore, as shown in the Book of Job, Satan is an Angel of the Lord who is still doing his duty. Christian lore makes him a rebel banished from Heaven who hates God and is making war on Him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T08:59:35-07:00","id":987281,"title":"","content":"You're right. There is an actual difference in the way Satan is treated in the two religions. But in Scion, it's a fictionalized version of Satan and the myths only need to have a grain of truth in them. So my point is that Satan could be an archangel who is currently doing his duty. Everyone knows that one day his duty will become obsolete at which point he will rebel. Because of this inevitable betrayal (hopefully frequently portrayed using toy dinosaurs), he sometimes does things that are subversive to the rest of the pantheon's goals (an example being the temptation of Jesus), but for the most part, until the seals on the book start to get broken and the four horsemen appear, he does his duty.<br /> <br /> It's not that different from Loki and Ragnarok.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1g_IC644YJoiVAm6ngqcBmsQtff2YYtd3pDbZpaOxx4o\" target=\"_blank\">My Exalted Character Creation Tool may be downloaded here.</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1086797-demac-s-exalted-character-creation-tool\" target=\"_blank\">The thread talking about the tool can be found here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1136654-exalted-seats-of-power\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted: Seats of Power is a homebrewed manse creation system.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1oaq3wk7lJKZ022SUA4iPfGzMpmBTNXlM\" target=\"_blank\">I have a rewrite of the craft system which can be downloaded here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1070312-i-got-my-book-it-s-super-fancy-and-i-can-t-read-the-cover/page2\" target=\"_blank\">I like the Mesoamerican look</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2346-demac","name":"Demac","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"385"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T19:03:57-07:00","id":987538,"title":"","content":"Or... possibly the original Samael died in a battle once and two of his scions fought over his mantel. The winner became Samael who is loyal to Jehovah and looser became Satan who lead a rebellion and/or joined/became a Titan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1g_IC644YJoiVAm6ngqcBmsQtff2YYtd3pDbZpaOxx4o\" target=\"_blank\">My Exalted Character Creation Tool may be downloaded here.</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1086797-demac-s-exalted-character-creation-tool\" target=\"_blank\">The thread talking about the tool can be found here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1136654-exalted-seats-of-power\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted: Seats of Power is a homebrewed manse creation system.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1oaq3wk7lJKZ022SUA4iPfGzMpmBTNXlM\" target=\"_blank\">I have a rewrite of the craft system which can be downloaded here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1070312-i-got-my-book-it-s-super-fancy-and-i-can-t-read-the-cover/page2\" target=\"_blank\">I like the Mesoamerican look</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2346-demac","name":"Demac","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"385"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T03:40:45-07:00","id":991325,"title":"","content":"Why not have the one God just be a angle? He could be the figure head father figure like zuse and he just decided to write himself in as a more prodomanent figure? I say that as they already point out that all the creation myths are true at the same time. So no reason another would be all powerful god can't be around. Then just have lucifer be his first creation and he fell. Falling in this case means he lost himself and became a titan or maybe he is still a god and just the opposition the the one god. <br /> You could easily make lower angels creatures and guides. Build a psp around major miracles in the Bible and for virtues you can have the oposing Duty vs Freedom. <br /> There is no reason to shy away from using God as anything other then a pantheon head.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6424-fuzzykuma","name":"Fuzzykuma","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T06:59:07-07:00","id":991375,"title":"","content":"You could save this for the community content angle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T14:00:00-07:00","id":993087,"title":"","content":"i'd go for divine council route if doing this pantheon. find someone from green ronin or paizo that has familiarity with the divine council version of angels and build the pantheon from that origin point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/885-bwgustaf","name":"bwgustaf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T15:25:00-07:00","id":993123,"title":"","content":"What about the idea of using God as a titan. Make him all biblical old school ultra strict and have the angel be the ones who created Jesus to be a replacement. Lucifer and the lords of hell as &quot;gods&quot; demons as monsters and then using the Arch angels and Jesus as &quot;gods&quot; for the &quot;good&quot; side.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6424-fuzzykuma","name":"Fuzzykuma","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T15:44:57-07:00","id":993143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fuzzykuma</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975893-brainstorming-for-an-angelic-pantheon?p=993123#post993123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about the idea of using God as a titan. Make him all biblical old school ultra strict and have the angel be the ones who created Jesus to be a replacement. Lucifer and the lords of hell as &quot;gods&quot; demons as monsters and then using the Arch angels and Jesus as &quot;gods&quot; for the &quot;good&quot; side.</div> </div> </div> </div>Titans aren't evil in 2e, and I'm not sure the secret to handling Christianity in Scion is &quot;completely change the Jesus myth.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T16:04:27-07:00","id":993154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fuzzykuma</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975893-brainstorming-for-an-angelic-pantheon?p=993123#post993123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about the idea of using God as a titan. Make him all biblical old school ultra strict and have the angel be the ones who created Jesus to be a replacement. Lucifer and the lords of hell as &quot;gods&quot; demons as monsters and then using the Arch angels and Jesus as &quot;gods&quot; for the &quot;good&quot; side.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If anything I would think God would be a Primordial, angels would be Titans (see: Nephilim argument) and honestly have Jesus as a Scion of Apollo or something. It's difficult because Christianity is the hardest thing to fit into Scion's cosmology, because a setting where gods are actually involved in lives of mortals means Christianity shouldn't have had nearly the 'clean sweep' that it did.<br /> <br /> So if you twisted my arm and made me center on it - 'GOD' would be a primordial, the angels would be Titans, and Jesus would be a Scion of Apollo who created his own pantheon, with Saints as the backup gods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T16:26:05-07:00","id":993163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975893-brainstorming-for-an-angelic-pantheon?p=993143#post993143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Titans aren't evil in 2e, and I'm not sure the secret to handling Christianity in Scion is &amp;quot;completely change the Jesus myth.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Not wanting to make god evil. Just a titan, someone lost in there nature and not really seeing humanity and interacting with them, or that seems to be the way they are having titans now to me. <br /> So in this case god just becomes the more hardass old god he was and can be so harsh because of his disassociation with humanity. <br /> Ironically you could use the events of Jesus as the event that caused him to dissisosiacte from humanity and the event that bring Jesus from Demigod to god level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6424-fuzzykuma","name":"Fuzzykuma","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T16:29:11-07:00","id":993164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975893-brainstorming-for-an-angelic-pantheon?p=993154#post993154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> If anything I would think God would be a Primordial, angels would be Titans (see: Nephilim argument) and honestly have Jesus as a Scion of Apollo or something. It's difficult because Christianity is the hardest thing to fit into Scion's cosmology, because a setting where gods are actually involved in lives of mortals means Christianity shouldn't have had nearly the 'clean sweep' that it did.<br /> <br /> So if you twisted my arm and made me center on it - 'GOD' would be a primordial, the angels would be Titans, and Jesus would be a Scion of Apollo who created his own pantheon, with Saints as the backup gods.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really, through history pantheons have risen and fallen and changed. God's get murged, surplanted and dumped all the time. If anything by the thought of more active gods then Christianity, judaism or any monotheistic religion would never come to exist. <br /> I think a large problem people have is stepping back and seeing modern religion as just another set of myths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6424-fuzzykuma","name":"Fuzzykuma","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T16:38:27-07:00","id":993173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fuzzykuma</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975893-brainstorming-for-an-angelic-pantheon?p=993164#post993164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not really, through history pantheons have risen and fallen and changed. God's get murged, surplanted and dumped all the time. If anything by the thought of more active gods then Christianity, judaism or any monotheistic religion would never come to exist.<br /> I think a large problem people have is stepping back and seeing modern religion as just another set of myths.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Judaism is anything <b>but</b> monotheistic, especially when you delve into Jewish mysticism or go further back. I'm not arguing that they 'don't' exist, so I'm pretty sure you misinterpreted what I said. What I said was that it makes no sense for you to drop a monotheistic religion into Scion that has supremacy over every other pantheon. People would stay involved with their gods because their gods would still be there to remind them they exist/give them culture heroes to survive. We already had the debate on merging gods in another active thread, and it simply doesn't happen in Scion the way it does in real life.<br /> <br /> It's ironic that you would say people arn't stepping back and seeing modern religion as just another set of myths, because if you actually do what you suggest you would see that the Monotheistic religions of our time are <i>not actually monotheistic</i>. That in mind, the suggestion I made is entirely possible - and even <i>reasonable</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T17:02:32-07:00","id":993179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975893-brainstorming-for-an-angelic-pantheon?p=993173#post993173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Judaism is anything <b>but</b> monotheistic, especially when you delve into Jewish mysticism or go further back. I'm not arguing that they 'don't' exist, so I'm pretty sure you misinterpreted what I said. What I said was that it makes no sense for you to drop a monotheistic religion into Scion that has supremacy over every other pantheon. People would stay involved with their gods because their gods would still be there to remind them they exist/give them culture heroes to survive. We already had the debate on merging gods in another active thread, and it simply doesn't happen in Scion the way it does in real life.<br /> <br /> It's ironic that you would say people arn't stepping back and seeing modern religion as just another set of myths, because if you actually do what you suggest you would see that the Monotheistic religions of our time are <i>not actually monotheistic</i>. That in mind, the suggestion I made is entirely possible - and even <i>reasonable</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll easily admit a lack of knoladge in most percoved monotheistic religions. However I don't think it's to hard to just have Christianity to be the big thing at the moment as humans change and change their minds. If nothing els the logistic nightmare of removing Christianity, at least for America as I am an American so I know how intrenched it is in my country, and replacing it with multiply active pantheons. That seems staggering to say the least! The whole of human history would change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6424-fuzzykuma","name":"Fuzzykuma","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T17:50:56-07:00","id":993194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fuzzykuma</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975893-brainstorming-for-an-angelic-pantheon?p=993179#post993179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'll easily admit a lack of knoladge in most percoved monotheistic religions. However I don't think it's to hard to just have Christianity to be the big thing at the moment as humans change and change their minds. If nothing els the logistic nightmare of removing Christianity, at least for America as I am an American so I know how intrenched it is in my country, and replacing it with multiply active pantheons. That seems staggering to say the least! The whole of human history would change.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why you don't remove Christianity from the states. You have a Christian Pantheon (Jesus + Saints) who serves the same purpose, with a majority of America focusing more on Jesus and a few other figures, whereas the East Coast and Catholic dominated areas fixate more on the Saints.<br /> <br /> Edit: Essentially, Scion is a game that is heavily inspired by works like American Gods, which focuses on different cultures bringing their gods with them into America, and how those gods still have a presence in their homelands. Any game or story that focuses on the Christian God disrupts those themes just because of how overwhelming the presence of Christianity in America and other countries is. If you <i>must</i> include it as an item of interest (which American Gods never does, even the new gods are things like The Internet), then it's preferable to do something like - make Yahwh/Jehovah/Allah a Primordial, make angels titans, and have Jesus be a Scion who borrowed from the mythology and formed his own Pantheon. It's the least disruptive tactic I can come up with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11726,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","user":"Solana","date":". 10-25-2016, 08:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T17:56:36-07:00","id":993199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975893-brainstorming-for-an-angelic-pantheon?p=993194#post993194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which is why you don't remove Christianity from the states. You have a Christian Pantheon (Jesus + Saints) who serves the same purpose, with a majority of America focusing more on Jesus and a few other figures, whereas the East Coast and Catholic dominated areas fixate more on the Saints.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why move God to a primordial? Would you not want to balance it out with demons and a devil figure as part of the pantheon? Why not use angels vs saints and have saint just be moretal people invested with legend by the new cult rules? What would you do with God as a persona?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6424-fuzzykuma","name":"Fuzzykuma","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T18:50:05-07:00","id":993227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fuzzykuma</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975893-brainstorming-for-an-angelic-pantheon?p=993199#post993199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why move God to a primordial? Would you not want to balance it out with demons and a devil figure as part of the pantheon? Why not use angels vs saints and have saint just be moretal people invested with legend by the new cult rules? What would you do with God as a persona?</div> </div> </div> </div>God as he is understood by modern day Christians is more of an all encompassing spiritual presence that embodies certain purviews, the angels likewise are described as lacking free will and are also utterly consumed with the roles assigned to them by God. Neall has stated that in Second Edition, Titans are not evil, but rather similar to old gods who at times take their purviews too far. Considering the children of humanity and angels are the Nephelim, which are described as giants and are often monstrous (to say nothing of their undead corpses) it paints a very strong picture of the angels being Titanic in nature. Because God is a described as an all encompassing presence that embodies Order and Love, that would make 'Him' a Primordial in the context of the Scion Cosmology we've been made aware of so far.<br /> <br /> Jesus and the Saints are scions that became gods, because they are worshiped in the same manner as gods (Brigid for example, in the Tuatha write up? In the actual mythology she didn't do much of anything. Everything attributed to her is essentially after she became a saint of Celtic Christianity, this is an example of how interchangable gods and saints are). This is also to account for Jesus being a much more 'human' and relatable figure than his father is. Picture ancient Rome, a time when the Greek/Roman gods were in full representation. Apollo has a son in a Jewish community. Scion of Apollo grows up, is disgusted with his lineage, and reflects that in the people of his birth there exists prophecy of a Messiah, he hijacks the Legend for his own and rises to prominence, making use of his father's Health purview and Leadership calling. Boom, you've got yourself a new pantheon there.<br /> <br /> If you go back far enough to the point where God is 'not' a Primordial, that'd be something closer to the Canaanite pantheon, which is going to get an official release sometime later.<br /> <br /> Edit: It bears repeating that titans and primordials are <i>not</i> necessarily evil. If you want to include demons and a devil figure, you're welcome to do so - although that entire dynamic was just stolen from Zoroastrianism, I'm <i>really</i> disenchanted with Christianity and the way it's grown from its roots in general. You could do it, though. Have a Primordial of Order raging against a Primordial of Chaos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11726,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","user":"Solana","date":". 10-25-2016, 09:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T20:11:38-07:00","id":994360,"title":"","content":"Can't say I agree with some of Solana's points, but I think that would end up being more of a distraction. I've seen a lot of debate on the theoretical discussion about the underlying philosophy behind an Angelic Pantheon, but very little actual nuts and bolts talk. So, atamajakki, have you seen enough to make an attempt at a pantheon? Do you think there's something of value worth pursuing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6942-simison","name":"simison","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6942_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T08:32:58-07:00","id":994604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975893-brainstorming-for-an-angelic-pantheon?p=994360#post994360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can't say I agree with some of Solana's points, but I think that would end up being more of a distraction. I've seen a lot of debate on the theoretical discussion about the underlying philosophy behind an Angelic Pantheon, but very little actual nuts and bolts talk. So, atamajakki, have you seen enough to make an attempt at a pantheon? Do you think there's something of value worth pursuing?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Nuts and bolts are a little tough at this point since we don't have the books yet. I have an Angelic pantheon marked out with Jahovah as the head of the pantheon. I've picked out several archangels based on Catholic and Orthadox Christian traditions and assigned some purviews and callings to them. These are, of course, tentative because we don't have many details on what those purviews and callings entail. I've named them &quot;The Adoni&quot; because Abraham repeatedly called Jahovah and his angels that attended him &quot;Lords&quot; and I think their psp is going to be something that's based on psalms. I'm planning on adding a few archangels recognized by Muslim traditions as well and I don't talk about Jesus at all. I think I'm going to treat him as an Incarnation of Jahovah if it comes up.<br /> <br /> I am using Samael and Lucifer as different characters. I think I'm going to with the idea that the original Samael died and two of his scions competed for the mantel. The winner took his father's mantle and the looser decided to lead a rebellion against heaven. I'm also going to have a titan called Beelzebub and another called Azrael.<br /> <br /> The driving force between making my angelic pantheon is that I have a player who wants to play someone that's part of the Catholic Inquisition. So basically what I'm going to do is have the Inquisition have been reformed in the 1800's to be a sort of black opps group that supplies support to Scions of the Adoni in their efforts against threats to humanity. They would essentially provide the same function and benefits for scions of the Adoni that a parent's cult would provide for scions of other pantheons.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I guess I should say plainly that the point of my efforts is create a pantheon that will let my player play the protagonist he wants to play and allow him to have fun with it. I find simison's ideas on making Johovah a primordial interesting but unless the rules in Hero give us a way to play titan spawn as PCs, then I'm going to error on the side of creating a pantheon that at least looks like other pantheons, even if the nomenclature is a bit different in that most of the &quot;gods&quot; are called &quot;archangels&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1g_IC644YJoiVAm6ngqcBmsQtff2YYtd3pDbZpaOxx4o\" target=\"_blank\">My Exalted Character Creation Tool may be downloaded here.</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1086797-demac-s-exalted-character-creation-tool\" target=\"_blank\">The thread talking about the tool can be found here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1136654-exalted-seats-of-power\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted: Seats of Power is a homebrewed manse creation system.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1oaq3wk7lJKZ022SUA4iPfGzMpmBTNXlM\" target=\"_blank\">I have a rewrite of the craft system which can be downloaded here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1070312-i-got-my-book-it-s-super-fancy-and-i-can-t-read-the-cover/page2\" target=\"_blank\">I like the Mesoamerican look</a>.","edited":{"userid":2346,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2346-demac","user":"Demac","date":". 10-28-2016, 11:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2346-demac","name":"Demac","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"385"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T10:36:56-07:00","id":994660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975893-brainstorming-for-an-angelic-pantheon?p=994360#post994360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can't say I agree with some of Solana's points, but I think that would end up being more of a distraction. I've seen a lot of debate on the theoretical discussion about the underlying philosophy behind an Angelic Pantheon, but very little actual nuts and bolts talk. So, atamajakki, have you seen enough to make an attempt at a pantheon? Do you think there's something of value worth pursuing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Can't say I understand the point of calling me out, and some of my arguments (without specifying which ones) before naming it a distraction and moving on. That's kind of hit and run, don't you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T10:55:32-07:00","id":994672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975893-brainstorming-for-an-angelic-pantheon?p=994604#post994604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The driving force between making my angelic pantheon is that I have a player who wants to play someone that's part of the Catholic Inquisition. So basically what I'm going to do is have the Inquisition have been reformed in the 1800's to be a sort of black opps group that supplies support to Scions of the Adoni in their efforts against threats to humanity. They would essentially provide the same function and benefits for scions of the Adoni that a parent's cult would provide for scions of other pantheons.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mentioned this in your character concept post, but this is really like asking us to accept a Neo-Nazi as a PC. Gonna make a lot of people uncomfortable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T11:08:59-07:00","id":994699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975893-brainstorming-for-an-angelic-pantheon?p=994660#post994660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can't say I understand the point of calling me out, and some of my arguments (without specifying which ones) before naming it a distraction and moving on. That's kind of hit and run, don't you think?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No, I don't. I've never actually heard of a hit and run used in a forum. I was simply transitioning from your point to addressing what I thought was a more important issue, which is why I didn't go into specifics. If you are feel slighted, I apologize. If you wish to discuss in detail, feel free to send me a PM.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6942-simison","name":"simison","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6942_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T11:10:47-07:00","id":994700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975893-brainstorming-for-an-angelic-pantheon?p=994360#post994360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can't say I agree with some of Solana's points, but I think that would end up being more of a distraction. I've seen a lot of debate on the theoretical discussion about the underlying philosophy behind an Angelic Pantheon, but very little actual nuts and bolts talk. So, atamajakki, have you seen enough to make an attempt at a pantheon? Do you think there's something of value worth pursuing?</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, neighbor - &quot;Can't say I agree with some of Solana's points&quot; and then refusing to discuss them is a bit of a metaphorical side-swipe.<br /> <br /> &quot;Gosh, isn't that person terrible - now on to our next topic.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T11:14:17-07:00","id":994705,"title":"","content":"I've made posts in the past that voice disagreement with others in general without going into detail before without issue. So, I wasn't expecting it to cause any issue. It's like managing a group session where you're trying to steer the group in a different direction. <br /> <br /> Again, I didn't intend offense, and I apologize for hurting without intending.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6942-simison","name":"simison","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6942_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T11:58:20-07:00","id":994727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jachra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975893-brainstorming-for-an-angelic-pantheon?p=994672#post994672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mentioned this in your character concept post, but this is really like asking us to accept a Neo-Nazi as a PC. Gonna make a lot of people uncomfortable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, how is an Angelic Scion player character associated with a contemporary form of the catholic inquisition made in the World specifically to oppose threats to humanity the same as a Neo-Nazi character? I am legitimately and unfortunately confused.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T12:44:04-07:00","id":994758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975893-brainstorming-for-an-angelic-pantheon?p=994727#post994727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait, how is an Angelic Scion player character associated with a contemporary form of the catholic inquisition made in the World specifically to oppose threats to humanity the same as a Neo-Nazi character? I am legitimately and unfortunately confused.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I can't speak for her, but I will try to offer my interpretation?<br /> <br /> I believe she's comparing making the Catholic Inquisition into a friendly organization funded by the Church (which is, presumably, okay with pagan gods and their get at this point, otherwise it'd be fairly disruptive to the rest of the party) to someone stating &quot;I sure liked the Nazi uniform/aesthetic, it would be cool if I played an SS Character, but nowadays the SS is less focused on burning Jewish/LGBT people, and more concerned with being Task Force Valkyrie.&quot; Based on the history the Inquisition had with mass murder.<br /> <br /> Again, not trying to call people who are Catholic Nazi's, just trying to interpret what she said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11726,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","user":"Solana","date":". 10-28-2016, 05:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T13:04:58-07:00","id":994770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975893-brainstorming-for-an-angelic-pantheon?p=994727#post994727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait, how is an Angelic Scion player character associated with a contemporary form of the catholic inquisition made in the World specifically to oppose threats to humanity the same as a Neo-Nazi character? I am legitimately and unfortunately confused.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Inquisition was little more than a bunch of either delusional or psychotic roving thugs who targeted the weak and powerless, often to steal their things.<br /> <br /> Recasting them as the good guys protecting humanity is a bit like recasting the Thuggee cult as a heroic Robin Hood-esque revolutionary outfit defending the common folk against the oppressive Raj.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":5226,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","user":"Jachra","date":". 10-28-2016, 04:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T14:04:26-07:00","id":994816,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't say they were delusional or psychotic. Their behavior was much too directed and focused to be mentally ill in that particular way.<br /> <br /> I mean using those terms as a way to indicate someone is evil is bad enough, but they don't really mean what they're often purported to mean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T14:41:03-07:00","id":994853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jachra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975893-brainstorming-for-an-angelic-pantheon?p=994770#post994770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Inquisition was little more than a bunch of either delusional or psychotic roving thugs who targeted the weak and powerless, often to steal their things.<br /> <br /> Recasting them as the good guys protecting humanity is a bit like recasting the Thuggee cult as a heroic Robin Hood-esque revolutionary outfit defending the common folk against the oppressive Raj.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just gave you a response in the thread you mentioned but since it's turning into a thing here, I'll give the same response.<br /> <br /> A theme of the Christian religion is redemption. Taking something bad and making it good again. To say the character can't have his character concept because the organization did something bad hundred of years of ago is ignoring that theme. <br /> <br /> An excellent example of the theme at work from the Bible itself is when Saul, a man who hunted down early Christians so they could be executed by the Romans for their religious beliefs, had an experience with God, took on the name Paul, and went on to write many of the books in the New Testament.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I feel its better to let the player have what he wants and preserve a theme of the religion rather than deny the character concept and ignore one of the better aspects of the religion I'm trying to portray.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1g_IC644YJoiVAm6ngqcBmsQtff2YYtd3pDbZpaOxx4o\" target=\"_blank\">My Exalted Character Creation Tool may be downloaded here.</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1086797-demac-s-exalted-character-creation-tool\" target=\"_blank\">The thread talking about the tool can be found here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1136654-exalted-seats-of-power\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted: Seats of Power is a homebrewed manse creation system.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1oaq3wk7lJKZ022SUA4iPfGzMpmBTNXlM\" target=\"_blank\">I have a rewrite of the craft system which can be downloaded here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1070312-i-got-my-book-it-s-super-fancy-and-i-can-t-read-the-cover/page2\" target=\"_blank\">I like the Mesoamerican look</a>.","edited":{"userid":2346,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2346-demac","user":"Demac","date":". 10-28-2016, 05:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2346-demac","name":"Demac","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"385"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T14:57:47-07:00","id":994871,"title":"","content":"Solana; Jachra: I was wondering if that was roughly the perspective at play. I understand the opposition now, but I wonder if the point of view isn't a bit lopsided.<br /> <br /> Had Demac just said &quot;the Catholic Inquisition&quot; I'd find it questionable in the same breath, but the suggestion is of a hypothetically reformed Inquisition organized in a world where titanspawn and monsters are a tangible threat. It's true that the institution was historically a thinly veiled excuse for tyrannical and inhuman practices exercised to benefit those in charge, but it's not that organization that is wanted there, even if they would use the same name due to the connection to the Catholic Church and the ideological basis of resisting heresy; it happens that the heresy these people care about fighting is inhuman beings poised to be a danger to mankind, and that they would as a mission statement actually <i>care</i>.<br /> <br /> The church as an organ does not stand for the same values as when the real world Inquisition was formed either. I think it is burdensome to claim it's precisely the same as casting a genuinely damnable group in a good light when the subject of the matter differs starkly in function but identifies themselves by an common ideological function that was horribly misused in the past.<br /> <br /> Such a group would never be free of ambiguity regardless, because that is the nature of things and it would indeed be stranger if it was. How far would their nominal acceptance of other faiths in the face of priorities go if the correct circumstances to supplant them were presented? Cults of the pantheons all over the world presumably seek dominance over those which hail different gods even if their attentions are mostly turned to greater enemies. That the modern Inquisition could come into conflict with foreign Scions and their allies seems a feature inherent to the setting and not a bug.<br /> <br /> I can obviously only speak for myself, but the mentioned concept doesn't strike me as distasteful. Of course, there's not much arguing to have over how people feel (unless they're somehow objecting to unalienable human rights).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 10-28-2016, 06:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T15:00:53-07:00","id":994875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975893-brainstorming-for-an-angelic-pantheon?p=994853#post994853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I just gave you a response in the thread you mentioned but since it's turning into a thing here, I'll give the same response.<br /> <br /> A theme of the Christian religion is redemption. Taking something bad and making it good again. To say the character can't have his character concept because the organization did something bad hundred of years of ago is ignoring that theme.<br /> <br /> An excellent example of the theme at work from the Bible itself is when Saul, a man who hunted down early Christians so they could be executed by the Romans for their religious beliefs, had an experience with God, took on the name Paul, and went on to write many of the books in the New Testament.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I feel its better to let the player have what he wants and preserve a theme of the religion rather than deny the character concept and ignore one of the better aspects of the religion I'm trying to portray.</div> </div> </div> </div>Paul of Tarsus: Also oppressed women who wanted to teach within the Church. Not a fantastic example.<br /> <br /> Again, redemption is one thing, but the Inquisition's bad press isn't going to go away any more than did the Nazis.<br /> <br /> A <i>person</i> can be redeemed, Demac. An organization isn't a person.<br /> <br /> If you want a Catholic organization to hunt down monsters, I suggest picking something other than the torture maniacs, or making up a new one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":5226,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","user":"Jachra","date":". 10-28-2016, 06:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T15:01:03-07:00","id":994876,"title":"","content":"oWoD had its own Shadow Inquisition, which cared much less about, say, burning Jews and pagans than it did fighting the very real threat (in that setting) posed by the supernatural. I could very easily see Orders Militant being created in the World not to shield pilgrims from Saracen threats, but rather monsters and possibly Scions of the Mesopotamian Pantheon.<br /> <br /> I do think a name less tainted than Inquisition may be in order, likely just the Knights Something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T15:06:32-07:00","id":994882,"title":"","content":"As far as the name goes, I agree Inquisition is not the best for positive awareness.<br /> <br /> Knights Custodian?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T16:18:06-07:00","id":994930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975893-brainstorming-for-an-angelic-pantheon?p=994882#post994882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as the name goes, I agree Inquisition is not the best for positive awareness.<br /> <br /> Knights Custodian?</div> </div> </div> </div>Perfect, I love it.<br /> <br /> People don't use the Knightly orders enough. They know about the Templars and that's it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T16:54:48-07:00","id":994948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975893-brainstorming-for-an-angelic-pantheon?p=994871#post994871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solana; Jachra: I was wondering if that was roughly the perspective at play. I understand the opposition now, but I wonder if the point of view isn't a bit lopsided.<br /> <br /> Had Demac just said &quot;the Catholic Inquisition&quot; I'd find it questionable in the same breath, but the suggestion is of a hypothetically reformed Inquisition organized in a world where titanspawn and monsters are a tangible threat. It's true that the institution was historically a thinly veiled excuse for tyrannical and inhuman practices exercised to benefit those in charge, but it's not that organization that is wanted there, even if they would use the same name due to the connection to the Catholic Church and the ideological basis of resisting heresy; it happens that the heresy these people care about fighting is inhuman beings poised to be a danger to mankind, and that they would as a mission statement actually <i>care</i>.<br /> <br /> The church as an organ does not stand for the same values as when the real world Inquisition was formed either. I think it is burdensome to claim it's precisely the same as casting a genuinely damnable group in a good light when the subject of the matter differs starkly in function but identifies themselves by an common ideological function that was horribly misused in the past.<br /> <br /> Such a group would never be free of ambiguity regardless, because that is the nature of things and it would indeed be stranger if it was. How far would their nominal acceptance of other faiths in the face of priorities go if the correct circumstances to supplant them were presented? Cults of the pantheons all over the world presumably seek dominance over those which hail different gods even if their attentions are mostly turned to greater enemies. That the modern Inquisition could come into conflict with foreign Scions and their allies seems a feature inherent to the setting and not a bug.<br /> <br /> I can obviously only speak for myself, but the mentioned concept doesn't strike me as distasteful. Of course, there's not much arguing to have over how people feel (unless they're somehow objecting to unalienable human rights).</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not something I could run because of how uncomfortable I am with that sort of thing. To answer for my own purposes? It would offend me if things were portrayed as: &quot;Well the inquisition wasn't evil in Scion, because witches and monsters were actually real.&quot; On the surface it's an entirely valid point - there are monsters and sorcerers and witches in Scion. <i>Obviously</i> things would have gone a bit differently. It's a sensitive issue though, because if it were done that way it's almost a form of denial, which makes me very uncomfortable.<br /> <br /> But I didn't initially say anything because I assumed that Demac is planning on owning that dark history, and it seems my faith was rewarded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T19:23:34-07:00","id":995012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975893-brainstorming-for-an-angelic-pantheon?p=994948#post994948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not something I could run because of how uncomfortable I am with that sort of thing. To answer for my own purposes? It would offend me if things were portrayed as: &quot;Well the inquisition wasn't evil in Scion, because witches and monsters were actually real.&quot; On the surface it's an entirely valid point - there are monsters and sorcerers and witches in Scion. <i>Obviously</i> things would have gone a bit differently. It's a sensitive issue though, because if it were done that way it's almost a form of denial, which makes me very uncomfortable.<br /> <br /> But I didn't initially say anything because I assumed that Demac is planning on owning that dark history, and it seems my faith was rewarded.</div> </div> </div> </div>Glad to not disappoint. Yeah, I'm not in the business of glossing over the atrocities of the past or making apologies for the groups that committed them. I do understand why people would be uncomfortable dealing with something like that in their games, but honestly, it is something that my player would have fun with. If I was going to write this up for a larger group, I would probably include the inquisition along with some other options so that people could have more play options. But as is, they player specifically wanted to explore what it would mean to be a member of the Inquisition in The World so the options at that point are basically to say &quot;no, because the Inquisition did horrible things unlike all those other religions... oh wait....&quot;, say &quot;Yes, I'll let you play a member of a group that is currently engaged in horrible acts&quot;, or take the route I described where the Inquisition as having done all those things, but for the last 200 years the or so has changed how it operates to help people.<br /> \u200b<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1g_IC644YJoiVAm6ngqcBmsQtff2YYtd3pDbZpaOxx4o\" target=\"_blank\">My Exalted Character Creation Tool may be downloaded here.</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1086797-demac-s-exalted-character-creation-tool\" target=\"_blank\">The thread talking about the tool can be found here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1136654-exalted-seats-of-power\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted: Seats of Power is a homebrewed manse creation system.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1oaq3wk7lJKZ022SUA4iPfGzMpmBTNXlM\" target=\"_blank\">I have a rewrite of the craft system which can be downloaded here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1070312-i-got-my-book-it-s-super-fancy-and-i-can-t-read-the-cover/page2\" target=\"_blank\">I like the Mesoamerican look</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2346-demac","name":"Demac","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"385"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T21:23:30-07:00","id":995065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975893-brainstorming-for-an-angelic-pantheon?p=994948#post994948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not something I could run because of how uncomfortable I am with that sort of thing. To answer for my own purposes? It would offend me if things were portrayed as: &quot;Well the inquisition wasn't evil in Scion, because witches and monsters were actually real.&quot; On the surface it's an entirely valid point - there are monsters and sorcerers and witches in Scion. <i>Obviously</i> things would have gone a bit differently. It's a sensitive issue though, because if it were done that way it's almost a form of denial, which makes me very uncomfortable.<br /> <br /> But I didn't initially say anything because I assumed that Demac is planning on owning that dark history, and it seems my faith was rewarded.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course, yes. I was only saying as much as I did because I didn't think anything about the suggestion was meant to justify the historical precedents of the inquisition or present itself as apologist of them. Denying or whitewashing the atrocities of the past is not something anyone here wants to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 10-29-2016, 12:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}